  ('169c8722-4d0c-50a7-883d-52100164140f'::uuid, 'bcn-punta-san-carlos', 'insert_new', 'Punta San Carlos', 'punta-san-carlos', 'Municipio de San Quintín', 'Baja California', 'Mexico', 'Baja Norte', 'America/Tijuana', 29.602, -115.5, 'point', 'advanced', ARRAY['urchins', 'rocks', 'rips', 'isolation']::text[], ARRAY['reef', 'point']::text[], ARRAY['urchins', 'rocks', 'rips', 'isolation', 'Legal access and parking have not been field verified', 'Hazards and local conditions may change; verify locally', 'Map pin is generalized and is not a navigation or access point']::text[], 'Punta San Carlos is a point surf spot near Municipio de San Quintín, Baja California, Mexico. The source profile describes it as exposed and fairly consistent. Reported waves run left and right.', 'Reach the area via Mexico 1, turning off past El Rosario toward Punta Baja and continuing roughly 22km to the unmarked dirt track. Expect two hours of rough road, a 4WD is strongly recommended in the rainy season as routes change after rain. There are no facilities whatsoever: camping only. The small fishing village at the base of the point has no supplies. Carry all water, fuel, and food. Hazards include urchins, exposed reef and rock, and rip currents.', 'The source reports SW as the ideal swell direction; this is a soft directional prior, not a validated acceptance window. Reported offshore wind is NE.', 'Very rarely crowded', 'Static source guidance only. Check the live Quiver forecast and local conditions before paddling out.', ARRAY[6, 7, 8]::integer[], 45, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 180, 292, 236, 56, NULL, NULL, 'either', NULL, '{"version":"baja-production-enrichment-v2","usage":"editorial_swell_windows_with_session_calibration_pending","source_break_categories":["reef","point"],"source_quality_rating_5":2,"source_reliability":{"category":"fairly_consistent","ordinal_1_to_5":3,"interpretation":"Ordinal normalization of the source category; not a probability."},"source_exposure":"exposed","so